        <item>
            <title>0.15.84</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:02:55 +0100</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>245</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.15.84</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.2</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul>
<li>Quitting Corder, logging out or shutting down the Mac while recording now finishes and saves the recording first, instead of cutting it off.</li>
<li>Signing in or out during a recording waits for the recording to be saved before Corder restarts.</li>
<li>Opening a second copy of Corder no longer cuts off a recording that the first copy is making.</li>
<li>If the disk gets nearly full during a recording, Corder warns you, and if it runs out it stops and saves the recording instead of silently recording nothing.</li>
<li>If your session expires in the middle of a recording or transcription, the meeting stays complete and in the right place.</li>
<li>Opening a meeting while it is still recording no longer leaves it with a cut-short playback file; playback becomes available as soon as the recording stops.</li>
<li>Playing a video while it is being prepared from several places at once no longer prepares it twice.</li>
<li>If Corder can&#x27;t open its library (for example on a full disk), it now explains what to do instead of quitting without a word, and it never replaces your library with an empty one.</li>
<li>Deleting a meeting while it is transcribing stops the transcription, and deleted meetings no longer leave downloaded copies behind.</li>
<li>An interrupted download or share no longer leaves a broken copy that later downloads reuse.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
